    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "True or False? Let $A$ and $B$ be sets in a universal set $U$.\n\n$(A\\cap B)\\cup(A\\cap\\overline B)=A$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "True.",
      "worked": "True. $A\\cap B$ contains the elements of $A$ inside $B$, and $A\\cap\\overline B$ contains those outside $B$. Together these two parts contain all and only the elements of $A$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
